{
  "id": "T-1487",
  "created_at": 1790881002.9661188,
  "parent": "T-1483",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: fix round 1 for T-1484: write the three acceptance-named tests (session transcript preferred over newest; fresh session reports None; CLI forwards --transcript/--session-id)",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1484 (goal T-1483), branch cut from task/T-1484 (commit 0eb9268 implemented planner_context.context_tokens(config_dir, root, *, transcript=None, session_id=None), hook_message passthrough, cli.py --transcript/--session-id, and planner-prompt.sh forwarding). The gate held it gate_red because none of the three acceptance tests exist: `missing: test not defined` for tests/test_planner_context.py::test_context_tokens_prefers_session_transcript_over_newest, tests/test_planner_context.py::test_fresh_session_reports_none_not_another_sessions_size and tests/test_cli.py::test_planner_context_hook_passes_transcript_and_session_id.\n\nWrite exactly those three tests, named exactly like that, as unittest.TestCase methods next to the existing tests in each file, using the same fixtures (tests/test_planner_context.py builds a projects dir with transcripts; tests/test_cli.py patches sys.argv and the planner_context functions). Behaviour under test is the T-1484 spec: (1) two transcripts, the newer recording 190000 context tokens, the older named <sid>.jsonl recording 40000: context_tokens(config_dir, root, session_id=sid) == 40000, context_tokens(config_dir, root, transcript=<older path>) == 40000, context_tokens(config_dir, root) == 190000 (legacy); (2) with the newer 190000 transcript present, a session transcript without any usage line, or a session_id with no file, makes context_tokens return None and hook_message return None; (3) `orchestrator planner-context --hook --transcript P --session-id S` forwards transcript=P and session_id=S to planner_context.hook_message (patched) and prints its return value; without the flags both are None. If a test exposes a defect in the implementation, fix it in the three source files (in scope) and say so in the result. Do not rename or weaken existing tests.\n\nCommit first, then run tests/test_planner_context.py and tests/test_cli.py in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1486"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_planner_context.py::test_context_tokens_prefers_session_transcript_over_newest: passes",
    "tests/test_planner_context.py::test_fresh_session_reports_none_not_another_sessions_size: passes",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_planner_context_hook_passes_transcript_and_session_id: passes",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "tests/test_planner_context.py",
    "tests/test_cli.py",
    "orchestrator/planner_context.py",
    "orchestrator/cli.py",
    ".claude/hooks/planner-prompt.sh"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
