      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "The three acceptance tests exist as unittest methods with the exact names and cover the specified behaviours. I ran tests/test_planner_context.py and tests/test_cli.py in T-1484 with PYTHONPATH=tests and all 50 tests pass. The implementation passes transcript and session_id through context_tokens, hook_message, the CLI and the hook script. A missing transcript or session file returns None rather than falling back to the newest transcript, and the legacy no-argument call still returns the newest. The one remaining concern is low severity: session_id is interpolated into a path without validation.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/planner_context.py",
            "line": 33,
            "issue": "session_id comes from hook input and is interpolated into a path (directory / f\"{session_id}.jsonl\") without validation, so a value containing '../' can point outside the project transcripts directory. The same applies to the unconstrained --transcript path. The code only reads usage integers and returns a number, so impact is limited. Consider rejecting session ids that contain a path separator.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
